Generate a flowchart that guides the selection of meal options based on dietary restrictions and preferences. The chart begins with a general inquiry about dietary restrictions and branches into specific paths for vegetarian, vegan, and non-vegetarian diets, considering gluten-free requirements. Each path concludes with a set of meal recommendations tailored to the individual's dietary needs.

The diagram language used is Mermaid.

The diagram defines a decision-making process involving dietary preferences and restrictions. It starts with a question about whether an individual has dietary restrictions, leading to further questions about vegetarian or vegan preferences and the need for gluten-free meals. Based on the answers, it categorizes individuals into different dietary options: Vegetarian, Vegan, Gluten-Free Vegetarian, Non Gluten-Free Vegetarian, Gluten-Free Vegan, Non Gluten-Free Vegan, Gluten-Free Non-Vegetarian, and Non Gluten-Free Non-Vegetarian. Each category is associated with specific meal options.

The graph data is shown below:

{
  "Decision Tree": {
    "Start": {
      "Question": "Does the individual have any dietary restrictions?",
      "Yes": {
        "Question": "Is the individual vegetarian or vegan?",
        "Vegetarian": {
          "Question": "Does the individual require gluten-free meals?",
          "Yes": {
            "Meal Options": ["Gluten-Free Quinoa Salad", "Vegetable Stir-Fry with Rice"]
          },
          "No": {
            "Meal Options": ["Lentil Soup", "Vegetable Pasta", "Cheese Sandwich"]
          }
        },
        "Vegan": {
          "Question": "Does the individual require gluten-free meals?",
          "Yes": {
            "Meal Options": ["Gluten-Free Chickpea Salad", "Tofu Stir-Fry with Rice"]
          },
          "No": {
            "Meal Options": ["Vegan Bean Chili", "Quinoa and Vegetable Stew"]
          }
        }
      },
      "No": {
        "Question": "Does the individual require gluten-free meals?",
        "Yes": {
          "Meal Options": ["Gluten-Free Chicken and Rice", "Grilled Fish with Vegetables"]
        },
        "No": {
          "Meal Options": ["Chicken Curry with Rice", "Beef Stew with Potatoes", "Fish Tacos"]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

The diagram features rectangular nodes with varying background colors to distinguish between questions, options, and meal categories. The nodes are connected by directional lines with arrows indicating the flow of decisions. The lines are uniformly styled, and the text within the nodes is centered. The layout is hierarchical, with the main question at the top and branching paths leading to specific meal recommendations at the bottom. The color scheme includes shades of pink and red, with distinct border colors to enhance readability.

